// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Set Right What Once Went Wrong
// @category Time Travel / Speculative Fiction
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Set_Right_What_Once_Went_Wrong
// @domain   Narrative
// @scale    arc
// @version  1.0
// @engine   >= 0.8.1   (S23 story-time: chron `~>` + before())
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): the heroic MUTABLE-timeline subgenre — a traveller reaches into the past on purpose
// to repair a wrong, bettering the present that follows. (Quantum Leap: "to put right what once went wrong.")
//
// @model    Presentation-time is the spine; chron supplies world-line continuity. The discriminator is a
//           deliberate repair of an EARLIER wrong — `before($wrong, $fix)` re-checks that the mended wrong
//           precedes the mending in story-time. The benevolent inverse of the Grandfather Paradox (a change
//           that betters the one timeline, rather than self-erasing it).


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"

assoc set_right_what_once_went_wrong -> [
  grandfather_paradox : "the benevolent inverse of the self-negating change in",
  alternate_timeline : "betters the one timeline rather than branching, unlike"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// — founded here (the purposeful repair of a past wrong is the discriminator; promotion model) —
verb Mends(wrong) [+Temporal]   // reaches into the past to repair a wrong, changing the timeline for the better

imply SetRightWhatOnceWentWrong -> [Temporal, Redemption, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule (arc scale): a traveller MENDS an earlier wrong — the agent bound on a [&Mends] event (the
// recall anchor) whose `wrong=` names a past harm that `before($wrong, $fix)` places earlier in story-time
// (S23). Reaching back ON PURPOSE to better the present is the discriminator: parts it from the Grandfather
// Paradox (an accidental self-erasing change) and from any ordinary present-tense fix (no past reached into).
rule Set_Right_What_Once_Went_Wrong {
  when:
    char $traveller
    obj  $wrong
    evt  $fix [&Mends(agent=$traveller, wrong=$wrong)]
    before($wrong, $fix)
  then:
    $fix [+SetRightWhatOnceWentWrong]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Quantum Leap — Sam Beckett (TV, 1989–1993) ===
// Sam Beckett leaps from life to life through his own lifetime, landing in another person's shoes at the
// hinge of some past wrong — a marriage about to break, a death about to happen, an injustice about to land —
// and cannot leap onward until he has reached in and set it right, bettering the history that follows. "Putting
// right what once went wrong," week after week.

// SAM BECKETT — the traveller who lands at the hinge of a past wrong to repair it
char sam [+Protagonist]

// THE WRONG — the past harm he reaches back to mend
obj the_wrong

// in-world order: the wrong lies earlier than the mending that reaches back to it
chron the_wrong_done ~> the_leap_in

// THE WRONG AS IT FELL — positioned earlier than the leap-in that reaches back to mend it
scene the_wrong_itself @@ the_wrong_done {
  beat 1 {
    the_wrong [#Doomed]   // the harm as it first happened — earlier in story-time than Sam's mending
  }
}

scene the_repair @@ the_leap_in {
  beat 1 {
    // he reaches into the earlier wrong and sets it right, bettering the present that follows
    evt the_setting_right [&Mends(agent=sam, wrong=the_wrong)]
    // Set_Right_What_Once_Went_Wrong -> the_setting_right [+SetRightWhatOnceWentWrong]
  }
}
